mprehensive explanation of how humans experience music and to unravel the mystery of our perennial love affair with it. Using musical examples from Bach to the Beatles, Levitin reveals the role of music in human evolution, shows how our musical preferences begin to form even before we are born and explains why music can offer such an emotional experience. Music is an obsession at the heart of human nature, even more fundamental to our species than language. In This Is Your Brain On Music Levitin offers nothing less than a new way to understand it, and its role in human life."},"table_of_contents":[{"title":"Introduction: I love music and I love science","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"why would I want to mix the two?","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"What is music? : from pitch to timbre","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"Foot tapping : discerning rhythm, loudness, and harmony","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"Behind the curtain : music and the mind machine","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"Anticipation : what we expect from Liszt (and Ludacris)","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"You know my name, look up the number : how we categorize music","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"After dessert, Crick was still four seats away from me : music, emotion, and the reptilian brain","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"What makes a musician? : expertise dissected","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"My favorite things : why do we like the music we like?","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"title":"The music instinct : evolution's #1 hit.","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"subjects":["Music","Psychological aspects","Psychology"],"title":"This is your brain on music","subtitle":"understanding a human obsession","by_statement":"Daniel Levitin","publishers":["Atlantic"],"publish_places":["London"],"isbn_10":["1843547163"],"isbn_13":["9781843547167"],"pagination":"vi, 322 pages","number_of_pages":322,"